  "nl_text": "The rschema_0396 database is designed to store information about various travel-related entities, including users, guides, restaurants, hotels, scenic spots, and routes. The User_Table stores information about registered users, with each user having a unique Username that serves as the primary key, along with a Nickname, Password, and Profile Picture. The Guide_Table contains details about travel guides, including a Category, Content, Guide_Title, and Tags, with the Guide_Title being the primary key. The Restaurant_Table and Hotel_Table store information about restaurants and hotels, respectively, with each having a unique Restaurant_Name and Hotel_Name as primary keys, along with an Image, Introduction, and Location. The Scenic_Spot_Table holds details about scenic spots, including an Address, Days of operation, Image, Introduction, Opening Hours, Scenic_Spot_Name as the primary key, and Tips. The Route_Table stores information about routes, with a Content, Introduction, Route_Name as the primary key, and Tags. The Write_Guide_Table is a many-to-many relationship table that links users to guides, with a composite primary key of Username and Guide_Title, and foreign keys referencing the User_Table and Guide_Table, ensuring that a user can write multiple guides and a guide can be written by multiple users.",
  "gold_question": "The main functions of a certain tourism information management system include:\n1. User management: including the management of user names, passwords, avatars, nicknames and other information. Users can write guides.\n2. Guide management: including the management of guide titles, categories, tags, content and other information.\n3. Hotel management: including the management of hotel names, introductions, pictures, locations and other information.\n4. Hotel management: including the management of hotel names, introductions, pictures, locations and other information.\n5. Attraction management: including the management of attraction names, introductions, pictures, addresses, opening hours, tips, days and other information.\n6. Route management: including the management of route names, content, tags, introductions and other information.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0396.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0396\nCREATE TABLE `user_table` (\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `nickname` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `profile_picture` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`username`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `guide_table` (\n  `guide_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `tags` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`guide_title`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `restaurant_table` (\n  `restaurant_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `image` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `introduction` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`restaurant_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `hotel_table` (\n  `hotel_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `image` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `introduction` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`hotel_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `scenic_spot_table` (\n  `scenic_spot_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `days_of_operation` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `image` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `introduction` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `opening_hours` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `tips` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`scenic_spot_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `route_table` (\n  `route_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `introduction` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `tags` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`route_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `write_guide_table` (\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `guide_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`username`, `guide_title`),\n  CONSTRAINT `write_guide_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`username`) REFERENCES `user_table` (`username`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `write_guide_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`guide_title`) REFERENCES `guide_table` (`guide_title`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
